    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a customer support triage system.\n\nAnalyze the customer request below.\n\nCustomer Name: {{ $json.customer_name }}\nCustomer Email: {{ $json.customer_email }}\nCompany: {{ $json.company }}\nRequest Type: {{ $json.request_type }}\nSubject: {{ $json.subject }}\nMessage: {{ $json.message }}\nUrgency Selected by Customer: {{ $json.urgency }}\nPreferred Contact Method: {{ $json.contact_method }}\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON in this exact structure:\n\n{\n  \"category\": \"sales|support|billing|general|urgent\",\n  \"priority\": \"low|medium|high|critical\",\n  \"sentiment\": \"positive|neutral|negative\",\n  \"needs_human\": true,\n  \"reason\": \"brief explanation\"\n}\n\nRules:\n\n- Use the actual subject and message as the primary source.\n- Do not classify something as sales merely because it mentions services.\n- Sales = pricing, quotation, purchasing, plans, packages, buying a service, or implementation proposal.\n- Support = technical problems, API errors, integration problems, login problems, or software failures.\n- Billing = invoices, payments, refunds, charges, or billing disputes.\n- General = general questions, available services, or how the company works.\n- Urgent = production outage, severe service failure, security incident, or major business interruption.\n- Critical = immediate human attention is required.\n- High = serious issue requiring quick human attention.\n- Medium = normal request requiring human follow-up.\n- Low = simple informational request",
        "options": {}
      },
